.TH BUCKYBOI 1 "2026-09-20" "buckyboi" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
buckyboi \- Linux desktop overlay buddy (gaze, gesture, local identity)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B buckyboi
[\fB\-\-wake\fR|\fB\-\-quit\fR|\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B buckyboi
draws a rotating wireframe icosahedron as a fullscreen transparent
click-through overlay. On Wayland it uses wlr-layer-shell (Hyprland /
Omarchy / other wlroots). On X11 it uses Shape + XFixes.
.PP
Looking at the buddy (webcam gaze) or clicking it can enter Listening
if the local identity gate allows. Profiles and settings live under
.I ~/.config/buckyboi/
and never leave the machine.
.PP
This package ships the
.B default-features
binary (overlay + V4L2 gaze). Face / hands / voice ONNX backends are
compile-time features and are
.B not
bundled. Model weights are
.B not
included; use
.I /usr/share/buckyboi/download-models.sh
or the script from the source tree.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B buckyboi
Run the overlay (needs \fIWAYLAND_DISPLAY\fR or \fIDISPLAY\fR).
.TP
.B buckyboi \-\-wake
Wake a hidden instance via \fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/buckyboi.sock\fR.
.TP
.B buckyboi \-\-quit
Ask a running instance to exit.
.TP
.B buckyboi \-h\fR, \fBbuckyboi \-\-help
Print usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Prefer native Wayland layer-shell.
.TP
.B DISPLAY
X11 / XWayland fallback.
.TP
.B BUCKYBOI_DISPLAY
.BR wayland ", " x11 ", or " auto .
.TP
.B BUCKYBOI_CAMERA
V4L2 device (default \fI/dev/video0\fR).
.TP
.B BUCKYBOI_NO_CAMERA
Skip the webcam.
.TP
.B BUCKYBOI_MODELS
Directory of optional ONNX weights.
.TP
.B BUCKYBOI_SOCK
Control socket (default \fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/buckyboi.sock\fR).
.PP
\fIBUDDY_*\fR names still work as aliases. See the project README for
the full list (\fIBUCKYBOI_LISTEN_MS\fR, \fIBUCKYBOI_FACE_SIM\fR, …).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/buckyboi/settings.ini
UX settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/buckyboi/profiles.json
Enrolled people and embeddings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/buckyboi/models/
Optional ONNX weights (not packaged).
.TP
.I /usr/share/buckyboi/hyprland.conf
Hyprland snippet. Source or merge into your config; do not replace
.IR ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf .
.SH SEE ALSO
Project README and
.IR contrib/omarchy/hyprland.conf .
.SH BUGS
Gaze is a face-in-frame proxy, not a calibrated eye tracker. Face and
voice prints fail closed and will false-reject in bad light or noise.
Do not use this as a lock screen.
